The cube's 24 rotations are themselves generated in code by closing two quarter turns under composition, and two guards keep the closure honest: exactly 24 elements, and every element sends opposite faces to opposite faces, so the closure never wanders into the 48-element full octahedral group. The cycle-count arithmetic is the cycle index evaluated at $k^1, k^2, ...$, which is where Polya enumeration generalizes counting to inventory. The algorithmic side, gcd-class necklace sums and bracelet reflections, is #xref-to("dsa", "combinatorics") territory.

