Chapter 16 asked what a group is; this chapter asked what groups do to each other and to sets: maps preserving tables, quotients by normal subgroups, products with lcm arithmetic, fields from polynomial quotients, actions with orbits and stabilizers, and one cyclic group whose logarithm prices a protocol. #xref-to("math", "probability") leaves determinism behind next, carrying the counting habits built here straight into it.

